WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.787
For the environment, install only what the project actually needs.

00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:10.492
If you are studying orchestration only, Lang Chain and Lang Graph may be enough.

00:00:10.492 --> 00:00:19.212
If you are running the full Module 9 lab, you also need the integrations for Hugging Face models, Chroma,

00:00:19.212 --> 00:00:26.945
community tools, sentence transformers, Transformers, Accelerate, Duck Duck Go search, and the Chroma database package.

00:00:27.538 --> 00:00:30.545
Why separate the minimal and full environments?

00:00:30.545 --> 00:00:36.435
Because Lang Graph itself does not require a vector database or local language model.

00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:40.060
Those are capabilities you may plug into the graph.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:46.070
For a student project, smaller environments are easier to reproduce and debug.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:50.409
Do not install twenty libraries because one tutorial used them.

00:00:51.536 --> 00:00:58.320
Start from your architecture. Then install the integrations that correspond to the tools and models you actually chose.
